  Eve streams its own session protocol, not the AI SDK data stream that AI Elements is built on. The parts\
  look similar, and they are not the same type.\
\
  useEveAgent() from eve/react already reduces an NDJSON session into messages whose text, reasoning, and\
  dynamic-tool parts follow the AI SDK UIMessage shape. Eve\'92s own docs say those types are not\
  interchangeable with UIMessage, so an AI Elements chat would need a small adapter. Live subagent progress\
  is not inside the parent message. The parent emits subagent.called with a childSessionId, and the client\
  follows that child\'92s stream with streamSubagent().\
\
  That path would not show this app\'92s stack analysts. Those runs happen inside the harness, as separate\
  generateText calls. Eve only sees one run_pipeline tool call that stays open until the whole review\
  finishes. Moving the fan-out into eve subagents would be a second execution path, and the eval CLI is the\
  system under test.\
\
  The low-lift view is the harness trace that already exists. trace.jsonl records stage boundaries, and each\
  stack writes a finding file when it finishes. The report page already polls /api/runs/:id until the run is\
  terminal.\
\
  \'95 Add those events to the poll response: current stage, stacks finished, and the last few trace lines.\
  \'95 Render them above the report as a short activity list, then keep the ranked report as the finished\
    view.\
\
  Tailing trace.jsonl as NDJSON is the next step if the poll feels coarse. Token-level streaming, and an AI\
  Elements transcript, are a larger change: the model loop would have to switch from generateText to\
  streamText, and the UI would be watching model chatter instead of stacks finishing.\
