  Eve\'92s own trace tree, from the observability docs (https://vercel.com/docs/eve/observability), is\
  invoke_agent \uc0\u8594  agent.step \u8594  chat and execute_tool. A subagent is a linked trace\
  (eve.link.type=agent.dispatch). If this UI called the eve agent, you would see one run_pipeline tool span\
  that stays open until the whole review returns. The stack analysts are generateText calls inside that tool,\
  so they are not eve steps.\
\
  Open source that people actually use\
\
  The shared format is OpenTelemetry GenAI spans (gen_ai.*). Eve already emits those for its own sessions.\
  The AI SDK 7 generateText call this harness uses accepts telemetry and will emit the same kind of spans\
  once a tracer is registered. Backends that render that tree:\
\
  \'95 Langfuse (https://langfuse.com/resources/engineering/opentelemetry-languages) is the usual open-source\
    choice. Self-host or cloud, OTLP in, nested generations with model, tokens, and cost.\
  \'95 Arize Phoenix (https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix) is the usual local one. A single process, no\
    account, built for OTLP GenAI traces.\
  \'95 Braintrust, Honeycomb, Datadog, and Jaeger are the ones eve\'92s docs name as otelIntegration()\
    destinations. Braintrust is also a native Vercel trace-drain target. Those are products, not something\
    you drop into this repo.\
\
  OpenLLMetry will auto-instrument provider SDKs. It will not know what a stack is unless the span attributes\
  say so.\
\
  What I would use here\
\
  Gateway Live logs are the zero-setup check that GLM is still being called. They will not tell you which\
  stack, or whether stage 1 is stuck.\
\
  The view that matches this harness is the report page reading the files the run already writes: current\
  stage, stacks finished versus still in scope, and the last error. That is a poll of run.json,\
  scope_trace.json, and findings/, not a new tracing vendor.\
\
  A trace product is the step after that, and only if you want model steps and tool calls inside a stack.\
  Turn on telemetry in runAgent, tag each span with run_id and stack_id, and export OTLP to Phoenix locally\
  or Langfuse if you want it hosted. Eve\'92s Agent Runs stays the right viewer for the eve shell, and it will\
  not replace that until the stack loop itself is an eve session.\
\
